Changes of the size of the host's render buffer with a host framing, see test_2819 and #2819

A sphere is rendered with a film translate framing, then the host reallocates its render buffer to other sizes with
framings of the new sizes, and finally goes back to the initial size without framing. The render delegate must follow
the buffer of the host, and never resize it.
The scenario only runs with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last one is compared against the
reference image.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
